],"best_idea":"A third-person camera can run as two rates: the focus eases toward the hero on each fixed tick, yaw and pitch are velocities that ease in while a key or drag is held and halve on release, and the pitch floor rises fast and falls slowly with the terrain while the distance grows with pitch.","decision":"adapt","decision_why":"Centred orbit with no shoulder offset, no wall pull-in and no recentring, so it does not solve over-the-shoulder alone; the tick-stepped follow, the velocity input and the asymmetric terrain pitch floor are cheap shapes to take into the world camera, with the truncation fixed and a shoulder offset and wall pull-in added by us.","decision_status":"proposed","acceptance":"After a run up a slope the camera lifts over about 0.5 s and settles back over about 1.6 s with no jitter; a test feeding the same 1 s of input at 50 Hz and 144 Hz asserts the same camera pose within 1 unit.","camera_scope":"world"}
